    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d751">

                <pb facs="0790" n="778" xml:id="pg778"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">832.796/823</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Assistant Chief of the Division of
                        the American Republics</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Walmsley</hi>)<anchor
                        n="6" xml:id="d751-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-03-28">March 28, 1942</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The gist of Brigadier Gomes’ gratuitous remarks on Condor to me last night<anchor
                        n="7" xml:id="d751-f2"/> was: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>Condor, irrespective of origin or background, did and should still
                            render highly important service to Brazil.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>Condor has been for some time much more Brazilian than Panair.</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>It is Brazil’s prerogative to determine how Condor should be
                            reorganized to make it completely Brazilian.</item>
                        <label>4.</label>
                        <item>Condor is now making flights which are primarily of a military nature,
                            at his orders. Crews on these flights are by and large Brazilian reserve
                            officers and pilots.</item>
                        <label>5.</label>
                        <item>There are some sort of contract obligations which make it immediately
                            impossible to change the name; but eventually this should come.</item>
                        <label>6.</label>
                        <item>Brigadier Gomes expects and wants in due course our assistance in
                            technical aspects of operation and equipment.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <closer><signed>W. N. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Walmsley,
                    Jr</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d751-f1" n="6" type="source" xml:id="d751-f1-content">
                <p>Addressed to Philip O. Chalmers, Randolph Harrison, Jr., Philip W. Bonsai, and
                    Livingston Satterthwaite of the Division of the American Republics, and Laurence
                    Duggan, Adviser on Political Relations.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d751-f2" n="7" xml:id="d751-f2-content">
                <p>Brig. Eduardo Gomes was on an official visit to the United States at this
                    time.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
